---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Health & Wellness" description="Medical infrastructure near BARK, health plans, honest risks, and what to bring.">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative h-[45vh] min-h-[380px] flex items-end overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-accent/20 via-bark-800 to-bark-900"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-bark-900/90 via-bark-900/40 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 pb-12 w-full">
      <span class="text-label text-accent">Wellness</span>
      <h1 class="text-headline text-bark-50 mt-2">Health & Wellness</h1>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-bark-200 mt-2 max-w-xl">Medical infrastructure, BARK's health plan, honest risks, and what to bring.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Altitude Context -->
  <section class="py-20 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-6 reveal">Altitude: The First Question Everyone Asks</h2>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[1.1rem] leading-[1.85] mb-6 reveal" data-delay="100">
          Coroico sits at <strong class="text-bark-800">1,750 meters</strong> (5,740 feet). This is moderate altitude &mdash;
          comparable to Denver, Colorado or Bogota's suburbs. Most people adapt within 1&ndash;2 days with no symptoms at all.
        </p>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[1.1rem] leading-[1.85] mb-6 reveal" data-delay="200">
          The concern is not Coroico itself &mdash; it's the journey. La Paz's El Alto International Airport sits at
          <strong class="text-bark-800">4,061 meters</strong> (13,323 feet), one of the highest commercial airports in the world.
          Visitors typically spend 1&ndash;2 nights acclimatizing in La Paz before descending to Coroico. Once you arrive, the
          subtropical air at 1,750m is noticeably easier to breathe than the Altiplano above.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-bark-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden mt-10 reveal" data-delay="300">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8 text-center">
          <span class="text-4xl font-display font-bold text-accent counter" data-target="1750" data-suffix="m">0m</span>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm mt-2">Coroico elevation</p>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-xs mt-1">Most adapt in 1&ndash;2 days</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8 text-center">
          <span class="text-4xl font-display font-bold text-bark-800 counter" data-target="3640" data-suffix="m">0m</span>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm mt-2">La Paz city</p>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-xs mt-1">Real altitude sickness territory</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8 text-center">
          <span class="text-4xl font-display font-bold text-bark-800 counter" data-target="4061" data-suffix="m">0m</span>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm mt-2">El Alto airport</p>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-xs mt-1">Acclimatize before descending</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Medical Infrastructure -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Medical Infrastructure</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        What exists now, what's nearby, and what the limitations are. We present this honestly
        because healthcare access is a critical factor in any relocation decision.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <!-- In Coroico -->
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-10 reveal" data-delay="200">
          <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">In Coroico</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-lg mt-3 mb-4">Hospital de Coroico</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Basic public hospital in town. Handles common illnesses, minor injuries, and basic maternity care.
            Limited capacity, limited equipment, limited specialist availability.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Basic emergency care and stabilization
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Primary care consultations
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Basic laboratory and pharmacy
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-700">Limitation:</strong> No surgery, no imaging (CT/MRI), no ICU
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Surrounding area -->
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-10 reveal" data-delay="300">
          <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">Surrounding Area</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-lg mt-3 mb-4">Health Posts & Local Workforce</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Postas de salud (health posts) serve surrounding rural communities with basic primary care.
            Carmen Pampa University, 12 km from Coroico, runs a five-year nursing program &mdash; creating
            a local pipeline of trained health workers.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Rural health posts for primary care in villages
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Carmen Pampa nursing graduates entering the local workforce
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Traditional medicine practitioners in indigenous communities
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-700">Limitation:</strong> Limited dental care locally
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- La Paz hospitals -->
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-10 reveal" data-delay="400">
          <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">La Paz (3&ndash;3.5 hours)</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-lg mt-3 mb-4">Full-Service Hospitals</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For anything serious &mdash; surgery, specialist consultations, imaging, complex diagnostics &mdash;
            La Paz is the destination. The drive is 3&ndash;3.5 hours under normal conditions.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-700">Hospital de Clinicas</strong> &mdash; public teaching hospital, largest in Bolivia
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-700">Clinica del Sur</strong> &mdash; private hospital, modern facilities, English-speaking staff
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Full range of specialists, surgery, imaging, and ICU
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-700">Risk:</strong> Road closures during rainy season can cut access
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- BARK's planned additions -->
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-10 reveal" data-delay="500">
          <span class="text-label text-ember text-[0.6rem]">BARK Planned</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-lg mt-3 mb-4">What BARK Will Add</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            BARK's health infrastructure is designed to fill the gaps between what Coroico offers and
            what La Paz provides &mdash; not to replace hospitals, but to handle the daily and the urgent.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-700">Community health worker</strong> &mdash; one of the critical open positions
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              On-site first aid station with supplies for common injuries and illnesses
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Telemedicine via Starlink &mdash; remote consultations with specialists
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Emergency evacuation plan &mdash; satellite phone, dedicated vehicle always available
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Preventive Health -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Preventive Health</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        The best health plan is not needing a hospital. BARK's design prioritizes prevention
        through environment, nutrition, and community.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-bark-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Clean Water</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Independent water systems with filtration and treatment. Waterborne illness is a leading
            cause of health problems in rural Bolivia &mdash; BARK addresses this at the infrastructure level.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Nutrition</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            On-site food production means fresh vegetables, fruit, and protein year-round. The Yungas
            growing season never stops. Diet quality directly reduces chronic disease risk.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Active Lifestyle</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Community life at 1,750m with daily physical work, walking terrain, and outdoor living.
            This is not a sedentary environment. The lifestyle itself is preventive medicine.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Mental Health</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Community support structures, shared purpose, connection to nature, and retreat center
            practices. Isolation &mdash; the silent killer in modern life &mdash; is structurally impossible here.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Climate</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Year-round 18&ndash;19&deg;C average. No extreme heat, no extreme cold. No heating or cooling needed.
            The subtropical highland climate is one of the most comfortable on Earth for human habitation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Air Quality</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Cloud forest air, far from industrial pollution. No factory emissions, no traffic congestion.
            No local air quality monitoring data exists for Coroico, but the absence of industrial
            and heavy traffic sources suggests low particulate matter compared to urban Bolivia.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Honest Risks -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Honest Health Risks</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        No location is risk-free. These are the specific health hazards of the Coroico/Yungas area.
        We list them because informed people make better decisions.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800">Tropical Diseases</h3>
            <span class="text-label text-ember text-[0.6rem] shrink-0">Moderate risk</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Dengue fever and leishmaniasis are present in the lower Yungas. At 1,750m, Coroico has
            lower mosquito density than the lowland tropics, but risk is not zero. Dengue-carrying
            Aedes mosquitoes can survive at this elevation. Preventive measures: mosquito nets,
            repellent, standing water elimination, community vector control.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800">Venomous Snake Bites</h3>
            <span class="text-label text-ember text-[0.6rem] shrink-0">Low but real risk</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Fer-de-lance (Bothrops species) and coral snakes are present in the Yungas region.
            Bites are uncommon but can be serious. Mitigation: cleared paths, proper footwear,
            awareness training for all community members, antivenom in the first aid station,
            and emergency evacuation protocol to La Paz.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800">Landslide Injuries</h3>
            <span class="text-label text-ember text-[0.6rem] shrink-0">Seasonal risk</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            The rainy season (November&ndash;March) brings landslide risk throughout the Yungas.
            This affects road travel primarily but can also damage structures on unstable slopes.
            BARK's site selection will prioritize geologically stable terrain. Building codes will
            account for soil saturation and slope angles.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800">Limited Dental Care</h3>
            <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem] shrink-0">Ongoing gap</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Dental services in Coroico are minimal. Serious dental work requires a trip to La Paz.
            Preventive dental care and regular check-ups before relocating are strongly recommended.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800">Supply Chain Disruption</h3>
            <span class="text-label text-ember text-[0.6rem] shrink-0">Periodic risk</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Road blockades (bloqueos) are a Bolivian protest tradition. When the La Paz&ndash;Coroico
            route is blocked, medication and medical supply chains are disrupted. This can last
            hours to days. BARK mitigation: maintain a 3-month buffer of essential medications and
            medical supplies on-site at all times.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800">UV Radiation</h3>
            <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem] shrink-0">Daily consideration</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            At 1,750m with clear mountain air, UV radiation is significantly stronger than at sea level.
            Sunburn and long-term skin damage are real concerns for outdoor work. Sunscreen (SPF 30+),
            hats, and UV-protective clothing are daily essentials, not optional accessories.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Current Healthcare Reality -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Healthcare Reality Today</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        What actually exists right now in the Coroico area. No projections &mdash; just current facts.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-10">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-lg mb-4">What Exists in Coroico</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Hospital de Coroico</strong> &mdash; basic public hospital. Primary care, minor injuries, basic maternity. No surgery, no imaging, no ICU.
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Rural health posts (postas de salud) in surrounding villages.
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Carmen Pampa University (12 km) runs a nursing program &mdash; producing local health workers.
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Traditional medicine practitioners in indigenous communities.
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-700">For anything serious</strong> &mdash; surgery, specialists, imaging &mdash; La Paz (3&ndash;3.5 hours by road). Road can be cut by landslides in rainy season.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-10">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-lg mb-4">Environmental Health Factors</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              1,750m altitude &mdash; moderate; some studies associate this range with lower cardiovascular disease rates, though evidence is mixed and confounders are numerous.
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              18&ndash;19&deg;C year-round &mdash; minimal thermoregulatory stress.
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              No industrial pollution sources locally, though no formal air quality monitoring data exists for Coroico.
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              Year-round growing season supports locally sourced nutrition.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BARK Phase 1 Health Plans -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap mb-3">
        <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 reveal">BARK Phase 1 Health Plans</h2>
        <span class="text-label text-ember text-[0.6rem] reveal">Planned &mdash; Not Yet Built</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        What BARK intends to build first to fill the gap between Coroico's basic hospital
        and La Paz's full-service facilities. These are plans, not current capabilities.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-px bg-bark-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">Community Health Worker</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            One of BARK's most critical open positions. A trained health professional on-site
            for day-to-day medical needs and emergency triage.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">First Aid Station</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            On-site supplies for common injuries and illnesses. Three-month buffer of essential
            medications to weather road closures and supply disruptions.
          </p>
        </div>
